WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.520
It’s the mission of the century.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.450
A daring rescue into the depths of one of
the most dangerous locations in the multiverse:

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:12.369
Site 13, otherwise known as SCP – 1730.When
the impossible Site 13 was first discovered,

00:00:12.369 --> 00:00:16.380
multiple Mobile Task Forces were sent to plumb
its depths and none returned.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.940
They were greeted to a labyrinthine nightmare,
littered with deadly cognitohazards, escaped

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.220
SCPs, and mysterious, murderous leeches.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.340
Some were trapped, along with the civilians
they were sent to rescue.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.190
Others were killed or changed in unimaginable
ways.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:34.570
Mobile Task Force Apollo-3, also known as
“The Game Wardens”, had been sent in on

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:39.930
a rescue mission when they encountered a horrifying
sight: The captured broadcast of Bobble The

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.819
Clown, a dangerous SCP known for corrupting
and destroying children through its deadly

00:00:43.819 --> 00:00:44.819
messages.

00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:45.960
But this Bobble was different.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.409
Much like everything from Site 13, this Bobble
came from an entirely different dimension,

00:00:50.409 --> 00:00:55.219
and he had terrifying information to relay:
In the universe where Site 13 originated,

00:00:55.219 --> 00:00:59.530
the site’s psychopathic director, one Elliot
Emerson, had struck a deal with the Global

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:04.260
Occult Coalition – a controversial government
group who intends to “protect” humanity

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.940
by killing anomalies rather than containing
them.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:12.510
Emerson had converted his site into an unethical,
unrestrained slaughterhouse, and was incinerating

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.680
SCPs by the hundred in a so-called Body Pit.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.950
But Emerson’s game of death came back and
bit him, snapping the threads of reality and

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.920
turning the entire site into a dimensionally
displaced super-anomaly.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.390
The Game Wardens realized they were in way
over their heads.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.950
Their chances of surviving this place were
dropping by the second, and if they wanted

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.320
any chance of succeeding in their mission,
they needed backup, so Site Command called

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.450
in MTF Tau-5, aka “Samsara.”

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.430
Calling in Samsara for a run-of-the-mill collection
mission is like using a bazooka to kill a

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.340
housefly, but for a case as severe as 1730,
their skills were not only nice to have but

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.340
vital.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.910
Samsara are among the best of the best: Immortal
cybernetic clones forged from the flesh of

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:58.680
a god, equipped with weaponry and technology
that could surpass even that of other elite

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.270
Mobile Task Force units.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.580
The four members of Samsara are so adept at
what they do that they earned the nickname

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.240
“Power Rangers” among their peers.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.000
The remaining Game Wardens knew that with
Samsara on the case, they may actually survive

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.990
this thing after all, they just needed to
hold out.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:18.910
Samsara arrived on site not long after, packing
some serious technological heat – including

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:24.450
arm-mounted incendiary cannons, shock-absorbing
leg extensions, heat-resistant plating, and

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.510
built-in SCRAMBLE adaptations within their
eyes to ward off the deadly cognitohazards.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.130
Everyone involved was in for the fight of
their lives.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:37.069
The four Samsara agents – Irantu, Nanku,
Munru, and Onru – entered via a drainage

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:41.200
gate in one of the office buildings above
ground and began their descent inside.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.340
After observing numerous charred bodies, they
deduced that there must be a massive incinerator

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.670
somewhere on site.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.080
Emerson’s incinerator.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.230
Theorizing this was connected to the “Body
Pit” they kept hearing about, they descended

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.760
further, feeling the temperature rise as they
did so.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:03:00.150
Due to the anomalous nature of 1730, nothing
inside made any kind of logical sense.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.720
Caused by a reality-warping machine known
as THRESHER, the internal geography of Site

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.960
13 was subject to constant shifts.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.290
The team then split up to cover more ground
– Munro and Nanku continued to follow the

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:16.050
pipes and the heat towards the furnace, while
Irantu and Onru broke away to explore what

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.950
lay beyond a weak wall.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:22.020
After busting through the wall, Irantu and
Onru explored several empty office blocks

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.210
before finding their way into a control room
with a glass observation deck.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:30.190
While the window was obscured by garbage and
human corpses, signage indicated that the

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.230
incinerator and the body pit were directly
below them.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:37.650
The team once again reconvened, and managed
to activate the incinerator, which shredded

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:42.980
the mass stuck inside with several large turbines
before burning the resulting slurry, the same

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:46.670
process that had happened to so many anomalies
under Emerson’s watch.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:51.430
With the path cleared, Samsara decided to
descend via the incinerator, using the drainage

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.350
pipe as a kind of makeshift tunnel.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.800
Eventually, they happened upon the leeches.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:01.230
Large, black, and hungry, these creatures
seemed to infest 1730 by the thousand.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:05.290
Anywhere that blood or drainage runoff could
be found, the leeches could be found, too.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:09.300
They didn’t appear to have any connection
to an anomaly previously secured and contained

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.300
by the Foundation.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.349
They squeezed and wriggled through the cracks
in the walls, searching for fresh blood.

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:18.820
Onru detected that the leeches all moved with
a kind of collective purpose, suggesting a

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.560
telepathic hive mind.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:25.270
Onru was able to tap into this hive mind using
her cybernetic enhancements, and map the chaotic

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:29.380
geography of 1730 through the leech colony’s
collective knowledge.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.220
With this new advantage, they could add a
second goal to this rescue mission: Find the

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:38.210
THRESHER device causing all the instability,
and potentially reduce power to it if possible.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.000
But they were on the clock to save the other
survivors, as those leeches were sure to get

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.949
hungry for warm blood soon.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:47.750
They followed the leeches down the most direct
path towards the survivors.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.580
On the way, they encountered a horrifying
creature: The many-limbed humanoid nightmare

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.930
that functions as Emerson’s eternal punishment,
his charred body tied screaming and alive

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.580
to the platform where the monster’s head
should be.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.740
They managed to make it past the monster before
finally rendezvousing with Captain Hollis

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:08.340
of Mobile Task Force Zeta-9, otherwise known
as the “Mole Rats”, as well as the Game

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.050
Wardens and the other survivors.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:15.410
There were 27 surviving members of Site 13
staff, many of which had severe injuries – making

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.870
it even harder to transport them back to safety
through hazardous terrain.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.770
And to make matters worse, the leeches were
back.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.580
The team quickly decided that the best route
out of here was directly past the THRESHER,

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.850
where they could reduce power to the machine
for just long enough to create a stable path

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.850
of escape.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.551
Nanku opened fire on a hoard of approaching
leeches with a flamethrower, and everyone

00:05:34.551 --> 00:05:36.070
began running for their lives.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.900
It was a final, make-or-break dash to safety.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.949
However, their advance was soon stopped by
a strange, robed creature drawing a cognitohazardous

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:44.949
meme on the wall with its claws.

00:05:44.949 --> 00:05:50.510
When the team attempted to engage, it attacked,
exposing additional deadly memes and the dangerous

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.199
effects of its single white eye.

00:05:52.199 --> 00:05:54.669
And we’re not talking about internet memes
here.

00:05:54.669 --> 00:05:58.570
These are symbols and information that are
often deadly to even bear witness to, and

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:03.150
for you or I, this would be a real threat,
but not to a team equipped with goggles containing

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.440
cognitohazard filter technology.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:09.470
The battle was cut short when the floor collapsed
underneath them and this creature was devoured

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:15.199
by something even larger and more monstrous:
A gigantic black leech covered in huge, red

00:06:15.199 --> 00:06:16.199
eyes.

00:06:16.199 --> 00:06:20.770
Its entrance caused thousands of leeches to
spill out into the hall, as the monster screeched

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.040
and slithered its tentacles after them.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:28.400
Allow us to introduce you to Elijah, also
known as The Leech Boy, and a pivotal component

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.840
of the very existence of SCP – 1730.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:35.280
He was a boy with the mind of a toddler, but
he had the strange ability to absorb blood

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.470
through people’s skin – hence his nickname,
“Leech Boy.”

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:43.100
One of the doctors in Site 13, Dr. Hadley,
took pity on Elijah – after all, he didn’t

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.870
choose to be the way he was.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.310
Director Emerson didn’t share Hadley’s
sympathy.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:51.210
His orders to exterminate all anomalies included
humanoids like Elijah.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.710
When Hadley protested, Emerson had her beaten
within an inch of her life while other dissenters

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.710
were shot.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:01.500
Dr. Hadley, disgusted by the inhumanity of
her superiors, devised the perfect revenge.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.780
She sabotaged the incinerator and the body
pit, allowing a mass containment breach that

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.880
flooded the site with deadly anomalies.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:12.240
Young Elijah ended up consuming the slurry
of the other shredded anomalies, causing him

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.199
to mutate into a powerful monster, a behemoth
of a leech who gave birth to and controlled

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:18.199
all others.

00:07:18.199 --> 00:07:22.610
It was Hadley’s revenge that caused Emerson
to panic and activate THRESHER, leading to

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:27.320
the rift in reality and the creation of 1730,
and – by extension – all the problems

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.259
faced by our heroes today.

00:07:29.259 --> 00:07:33.100
Samsara and the others fled Leech Boy and
began taking a different escape route.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:37.520
However, while en route, they encountered
the dreaded Crystal Butterflies – a dangerous

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.900
SCP capable of destroying organic matter with
a mere touch.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:45.660
Irantu stepped up to bat, roasting the creatures
with his arm-mounted incinerator and taking

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.280
extreme damage to his body in the process.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.470
But they didn’t have time to rest.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.800
With the butterflies disposed of, they kept
moving, heading towards the THRESHER.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.300
But not all the SCPs were necessarily working
against them.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:00.190
Bobble the Clown came in handy at the next
checkpoint, manifesting in the monitor of

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.880
an electronic door and opening the way through.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:06.759
As they continued on their journey, they had
to fight off frequent attacks from leeches,

00:08:06.759 --> 00:08:09.350
losing some of the task force members in the
process.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:13.229
They were also forced to face off against
a number of other anomalies in order to survive

00:08:13.229 --> 00:08:19.949
– such as SCP – 2316 manifesting as floating
bodies beneath them, and SCP – 1370, which

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:23.610
used a huge, mechanized body to attack the
team of survivors.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.790
That was all just a warm-up for the true final
battle, though.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:31.000
The floor shattered beneath them, and out
of an impossibly huge chamber, the monster

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.820
that had once been Elijah wriggled free – reaching
for them with huge tentacles and shrieking

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.589
from its thousand-toothed maw.

00:08:37.589 --> 00:08:42.469
It was at least two hundred meters tall, and
barely reacted to any amount of firepower.

00:08:42.469 --> 00:08:46.680
It seemed like they were all doomed, until
Captain Hollis had a truly crazy idea.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:51.279
With the help of Samsara, she led the bloodthirsty
abomination down through the cryonics center

00:08:51.279 --> 00:08:53.640
and into an Olympia-class testing chamber.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:58.660
There, as the Leech Boy was bearing down on
them, Hollis opened the gates to two adjacent

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.180
containment cells, and something beyond incredible
happened.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:06.350
Two of the most powerful SCPs ever known – the
giant, sword-wielding gate guardian, and the

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:11.200
reality bending cosmic deer, SCP – 2845
– entered the arena.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:15.800
What followed was one of the most epic showdowns
in the history of the SCP Foundation, as the

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:20.010
Deer and the Gate Guardian went to battle
against the all-devouring Leech.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:23.320
While the monsters fought, Hollis ordered
her team to get the rest of the survivors

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:24.320
to safety.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.350
She and Munru of the Samsara team remained
behind to prevent any of the anomalies from

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:33.220
escaping as the entire base began sinking
into the ground from the combined forces of

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:37.530
the battle raging around them and the THRESHER’s
continued onslaught on reality.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:42.029
Even if the survivors escaped, would the anomalous
developments inside Site 13 escape and wreak

00:09:42.029 --> 00:09:43.630
havoc on the world at large?

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:48.459
That’s when Hollis received a vision, a
horrific, charred, post-apocalyptic world

00:09:48.459 --> 00:09:52.530
roamed by inconceivably powerful entities
and nightmare gods.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.760
It was a vision so horrific that just seeing
it nearly broke her mind.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:00.020
She knew what she had to do – the only way
she could truly defeat this terrible place

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.060
and ensure safety for mankind.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:06.090
While Leech Boy, the Gate Guardian, and the
Deer continued their battle for the ages,

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:09.340
Hollis ran to THRESHER and forced the machine
into overdrive.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:13.890
Up above, the remaining members of Samsara,
the Mole Rats, and the Game Wardens escorted

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.680
the survivors to safety.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:19.990
Downstairs, THRESHER emitted a blinding white
light as the system began to overload.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:24.540
In her final moments, all Hollis could do
was laugh – perhaps it was a laugh of pure

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.589
insanity, of a mind broken by the horror she
witnessed.

00:10:27.589 --> 00:10:31.610
Or perhaps it was a laugh of victory, knowing
that in spite of the immense powers all around

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.140
her, she had won the day.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:37.900
She had saved not only the survivors and her
teammates, but possibly all of humanity.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.820
And all it cost her was everything.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:44.790
Outside, the survivors had reached a safe
distance when the entirety of Site 13 imploded

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.649
in a final brilliant flash.

00:10:46.649 --> 00:10:51.610
When the dust cleared SCP-1730 was gone, all
that was left was an immense crater where

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.780
the impossible base should have once been.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.640
Captain Hollis had done it – through overloading
the THRESHER machine, she’d taken this anomaly

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.390
out of the world the exact same way it had
entered.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:04.620
It was torn from its moorings on our earth
and kicked into the infinity of spacetime,

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:08.360
perhaps never to be seen again, along with
everything it contained.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:11.000
SCP – 1730 was reclassified to “neutralized.”

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:15.470
Of course, the Foundation would have plenty
of other anomalies to pursue soon after, but

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:18.830
the nightmare of Emerson’s Site 13 was over
once and for all.

